    <section style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
      <h2 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.8rem; color: #0C1A24; margin-bottom: 1rem;">🐬 Ethical Dolphin Tourism — The Critical Issue</h2>
      <div style="background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.5rem;">
        <h3 style="color: #0C1A24; margin-bottom: 1rem;">The Problem: Dolphin Harassment in Kizimkazi</h3>
        <p style="color: #5c727f; line-height: 1.7; margin-bottom: 1rem;">Kizimkazi is the only place in East Africa to see wild bottlenose dolphins daily. But unethical operators use illegal methods: chasing pods with engines, encircling them, dropping swimmers on top of them, even feeding them. This disrupts feeding, nursing, and resting — and can drive dolphins away permanently.</p>
        <div style="background: #fef3c7; border-left: 4px solid #f59e0b; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0; margin: 1rem 0;">
          <h3 style="color: #92400e; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">🚩 Red Flags: Unethical Dolphin Operators</h3>
          <ul style="color: #78350f; line-height: 1.8; padding-left: 1.2rem; font-size: 0.9rem;">
            <li>"Guaranteed swim with dolphins" — wild animals can't be guaranteed</li>
            <li>Multiple boats surrounding a single pod</li>
            <li>Engines revving near dolphins, chasing them</li>
            <li>Dropping swimmers directly on top of pods</li>
            <li>Offering fish/food to attract dolphins</li>
            <li>No certified marine guide on board</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div style="background: #ecfdf5; border-left: 4px solid #059669; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0; margin: 1rem 0;">
          <h3 style="color: #065f46; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">✅ Our Ethical Dolphin Standards</h3>
          <ul style="color: #5c727f; line-height: 1.8; padding-left: 1.2rem; font-size: 0.9rem;">
            <li>Only certified operators with Zanzibar Marine Park ethical viewing permits</li>
            <li>Maximum 2 boats per pod, 50m minimum approach distance</li>
            <li>Engines cut or idle near dolphins — no chasing, ever</li>
            <li>Swimmers enter water quietly at safe distance — dolphins choose to approach</li>
            <li>Zero feeding, zero touching, zero harassment — ever</li>
            <li>Certified marine guide on every trip explaining behavior</li>
            <li><strong>Sightings NOT guaranteed</strong> — it's wildlife, not a show. We're honest about that.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section style="margin-bottom: 2.5rem;">
      <h2 style="font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 1.8rem; color: #0C1A24; margin-bottom: 1rem;">🐢 Turtle Conservation — What's Ethical, What's Not</h2>
      <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 1.5rem;">
        <div style="background: #fff; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; border-radius: 10px; padding: 1.5rem;">
